  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The empirical validation and mapping are limited to a single urban agglomeration, the Yangtze River Delta.",
      "what": "This study develops a novel method to delineate airport hinterlands by combining airport operational metrics with an adapted plume model. Applying this model to the Yangtze River Delta urban agglomeration, the research maps the service areas of regional airports, identifying PVG, SHA, and HGH as high-intensity point sources whose reach extends along ground transit networks into less competitive zones. It also introduces the concept of vulnerable hinterlands to pinpoint marginal, highly contested boundary areas.",
      "why": "The approach provides a systematic way to map airport competition and identify vulnerable market boundaries, offering planners a tool to prevent over-construction and coordinate aviation resources across dense urban clusters."
